 "text": "Hello, how are you doing right now? You' a great support, just being there for her in whatever language that's the strongest for you counts. Yes, it is. Lots of families do this, and it' wonderful one. Then watch her in the classroom, and ask her about it at mealtimes. She'll love showing off, and you' get a taste of the language without feeling like student. Some people do, unfortunately. But little effort now makes a big difference later, like traveling without bags, Try songs and riddles first, they' fun and everyone wins. And watch French cartoons together, they're great entry points. You do, and your daughter will pick it up without even realising.",
